+          <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.5-1">Occasionally, a command must refer to the entire gateway, rather than
+a termination within it.  A special TerminationID, "Root" is reserved
+for this purpose.  Packages may be defined on Root.  Root thus may
+have properties, events and statistics (signals  are not appropriate
+for root).  Accordingly, the root TerminationID may appear in:</t>
+          <ul spacing="normal" bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" pn="section-6.2.5-2">
+            <li pn="section-6.2.5-2.1">a Modify command - to change a property or set an event</li>
+            <li pn="section-6.2.5-2.2">a Notify command - to report an event</li>
+            <li pn="section-6.2.5-2.3">an AuditValue return - to examine the values of properties and
+statistics implemented on root</li>
+            <li pn="section-6.2.5-2.4">an AuditCapability - to determine what properties of root are
+implemented</li>
+            <li pn="section-6.2.5-2.5">a ServiceChange - to declare the gateway in or out of service.</li>
+          </ul>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-6.2.5-3">Any other use of the root TerminationID is an error.</t>
+        </section>
       </section>
